# Accessibility — component guidance

- Prefer semantic HTML (`button`, `nav`, `main`) before ARIA. Use shadcn primitives from `@/components/ui/*` — they ship sensible defaults.
- Every interactive control needs an accessible name: visible text, `aria-label`, or `aria-labelledby`. Icon-only buttons require `aria-label`.
- Images: meaningful `alt` from context; decorative images use `alt=""`.
- Keyboard: nested interactive elements inside clickable containers must not steal or bubble activation. Call `stopPropagation()` on click and keydown for inner controls; avoid putting buttons inside buttons.
- Focus: preserve visible focus styles (`focus-visible:ring-*`). Do not remove outlines without a replacement.
- Motion: respect `prefers-reduced-motion` when adding animations via `motion`.
- Tests: assert with `getByRole` and `getByLabel`; add `data-testid` only when roles are not unique.
